wer-fields 17592186108733] [17592186134384 :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f51a25843259881994e3dca0781b780878bec349930b76fbf449dc824e69ec2.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t) = ⟨2\\sin t, 3\\cos t⟩$ for $t ∈ [0, 2π]$.\nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$Area(D) = ∬_(D)(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} - \\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA = \\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2π}AAAAAAAdt$,\n\nwhere $P(x, y) =-y$ and $Q(x, y) = 0$. Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*"] [17592186134384 :question/answer-fields 17592186132313] [17592186134413 :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0$?\n\n$\\begin{vmatrix}A|= & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{3}; \\sqrt[5]{2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}0\\begin{vmatrix}, & B|= & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}4; 0\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}4\\begin{vmatrix}, & C|= & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}4; 2\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}4 \\mid$"] [17592186134413 :question/answer-fields 17592186132487] [17592186120452 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${7x - 2y = 10; - 2x + y = 8$.\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n$x = \\frac{D_{x}}{\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}}$, where $D_{x} =$"] [17592186120452 :question/answer-fields 17592186118796] [17592186115868 :question/problem "Find the product $E_{1}^{-1}E_{2}$, where\n$E_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, E_{2}|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186115868 :question/answer-fields 17592186114115] [17592186115891 :question/problem "Which of the following functions is not differentiable over the entire interval $x ∈ (-1, 1)$ due to the existence of a vertical tangent in the interval?"] [17592186115891 :question/answer-fields 17592186114253] [17592186069375 :question/problem "Select the function that is continuous at $x = 2$."] [17592186069375 :question/answer-fields 17592186067390] [17592186078996 :question/problem "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $[- 1, 2]$?"] [17592186078996 :question/answer-fields 17592186076724] [17592186097270 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{3}^{4}2x^{2}dx$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?"] [17592186097270 :question/answer-fields 17592186095514] [17592186234113 :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{l})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{l}=a+lΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-1}{n}=\\frac{1}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{l})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+l\\cdot \\frac{1}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{l}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186069405 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int2x^{2}\\sin (2x)dx$?"] [17592186069405 :question/answer-fields 17592186067570] [17592186097308 :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2(x - 1)$?"] [17592186097308 :question/answer-fields 17592186095742] [17592186083778 :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb30925ffaca0ce59de7508e0f3710fbb26f3a80dfbd80b689e9ee5a4cf7d699.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve $y = \\frac{x^{2}}{4}$ for $x ∈ [- 3, 4]$, as shown above?"] [17592186083778 :question/answ