uous on an open set $U$. Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x, y)$?\n\n1. $f_{x}(x, y) = x^{3}y - x$ and $f_{y}(x, y) = xy^{3} - y$\n2. $f_{x}(x, y) = e^{x + y} - 2y$ and $f_{y}(x, y) = e^{x + y} - 2x$\n3. $f_{x}(x, y) = \\sqrt{x - 1}$ and $f_{y}(x, y) =-3$"] [17592186125192 :question/answer-fields 17592186123722] [17592186134505 :question/problem "Given that $u = \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}$ is a non-zero vector that is orthogonal to the set $W = {\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}$, find the value of $\\frac{c}{a + b}$."] [17592186134505 :question/answer-fields 17592186133038] [17592186088290 :question/problem "The velocity vector $v = ⟨u, v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n$v = ⟨5t - 8, 2t^{2} + 4⟩$.\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$."] [17592186088290 :question/answer-fields 17592186086364] [17592186064952 :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in centimeters) at time $t$ seconds is given by\n$s(t) = \\frac{5t - 10}{t}, t > 0$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t = 2s$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186064952 :question/answer-fields 17592186063738] [17592186097359 :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n${x - 2y + z = 1; 2x - y - z =-1; - 2x + 4y - 2z =-2$\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [17592186097359 :question/answer-fields 17592186096048] [17592186180279 :question/problem "Let $R = [1, 3] \\cdot [1, 3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 10 - 2x - y$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$U(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"] [17592186180279 :question/answer-fields 17592186179188] [17592186152749 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)x^{2}yds$, where $C$ is the section of the polar curve $r = \\sqrt{2}$ for $-\\frac{π}{4} \\le θ \\le \\frac{π}{4}$?"] [17592186152749 :question/answer-fields 17592186150971]]
